<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>	   --SPECIAL REDEMPTION FROM PREPAYMENTS</p>
<p>MONEYS DEPOSITED IN THE SENIOR SPECIAL REDEMPTION ACCOUNT UNDER THE &quot;SPECIAL REDEMPTION - PREPAYMENTS, EXCESS REVENUES, DEBT SERVICE RESERVE FUND REDUCTIONS&quot; SECTION OF THE POS (P. 13) SHALL BE APPLIED TO REDEEM THE 1996 SERIES D SENIOR BONDS AS FOLLOWS: FIRST TO THE 1996 SERIES D SENIOR SERIAL BONDS, IN AN AMOUNT PRO-RATA TO ALL 1996 SERIES D SENIOR BONDS, AND SECOND AN AMOUNT EQUAL TO THE SPECIAL REDEMPTION REQUIREMENT SHALL BE USED TO REDEEM THE 1996 SERIES D 2027 TERM BONDS. AMOUNTS IN EXCESS OF THE SPECIAL REDEMPTION REQUIREMENT SHALL BE APPLIED BY THE TRUSTEE TO REDEEM 1996 SERIES D SENIOR BONDS, EXCLUDING THE 1996 SERIES D SERIAL SENIOR BONDS AND THE 1996 SERIES D 2027 TERM BONDS, ON A PRO-RATA BASIS AMOUNG MATURITIES.</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Friday, September 20, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on September 25, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. Inc.</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Grigsby Brandford &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
